  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening and extending social protection coverage</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While South Africa&#x2019;s social protection system is relatively comprehensive compared to many countries in the region, certain groups of people fall between the cracks for not meeting the eligibility criteria for social assistance. The Social Relief of Distress Grant (SRDG) introduced at the height of the impact of the COVID pandemic has been a temporary provision to assist such persons to meet their most basic needs. Government seeks to introduce a more permanent and sustainable income support system modelled along the SRDG for income compromised working age individuals between the ages of 18 and 59. Policy proposals in the green paper for comprehensive social security and retirement reform revised to demonstrate among others, financial sustainability for social security support, are still to be considered. The impact of the COVID-19 pandemic revealed structural weaknesses in the provision of health and safety in the workplace resulting in the revision of the National Occupational Safety and Health (OSH) Strategy of the National Department of Employment and Labour, and development of OSH guidelines for the informal economy.  The necessity to develop a communication strategy on communicable diseases for the informal economy also became evident during the pandemic. The impact of COVID19 has been and is still being particularly felt in the healthcare sector, necessitating continued interventions to improve the wellbeing of healthcare workers and the quality of healthcare facilities.  Additionally, work related injuries and disease data collection and reporting is fragmented. Since its introduction, the National Minimum Wage has not had a comprehensive monitoring and evaluation, yet if poorly implemented may have a negative effect on employment and possibly on wages.
The strategy will focus on technical, policy advisory, and capacity support to facilitate the finalization of the draft green paper and design of policy for basic income support; the development of a communi</narrative>
  </description>
